# A Y-up plate (P4-06 fixture for the `import` mesh branch): 20 mm across in x,
# 30 mm up in y and 4 mm thick in z, with millimetre numbers. `readObj` reads
# one body per o/g line, fanning each quad face below into two triangles.
# `e2e/import-mesh.spec.ts` imports it with Up "Y up" and gets a body whose y
# and z are the file's z and y.
o Plate
v -10 -2 0
v 10 -2 0
v 10 28 0
v -10 28 0
v -10 -2 4
v 10 -2 4
v 10 28 4
v -10 28 4
# The back face (z = 0) and the front (z = 4), then the four sides, each wound
# so its own normal points out of the plate.
f 4 3 2 1
f 5 6 7 8
f 1 2 6 5
f 3 4 8 7
f 4 1 5 8
f 2 3 7 6